description:
When the package is not loaded into the environment I get the following error:

``` r
iter <- flowery::generator({
  for (x in letters) yield(x)
})

flowery::iterate(for(x in iter){
  print(x)
})
#> Error in is_done(`_for_iter_2`): could not find function "is_done"
```

<sup>Created on 2019-04-16 by the [reprex package](https://reprex.tidyverse.org) (v0.2.1)</sup>

This PR adds `flowery::` so `iterate` works when the package is not loaded.
